-### SA-C01 — Narrow the local segment to a demonstrated inspection uncertainty
-
-**Verdict:** narrow. **Actor/task:** Maintainer adding utilities or changing shared implementation; separate reviewer and builder roles. **Conditions:** An unfamiliar or changed implementation leaves a concrete unresolved reuse/reference decision, including same-file scope.
-
-**For:** Repeated reuse prompts and reference failures support factual discovery as one possible burden. **Against:** Human abstraction choice and native success can dominate the task.
-
-**Failure:** An accurate candidate causes unwanted coupling or repeats a known implementation. **Weakest assumption:** Missing discoverable facts are the bottleneck.
-
-**Minimal test (proposed only):** Compare one real reuse task and one reference task with their recorded native plans, including intentional duplication; reject benefit when no correct additional decision or effort reduction appears.
-
-**Local/paid implication:** Local factual inspection remains free; this segment identifies no buyer.
